Be7 9. Rc1 f6 10. Na4 Na6 11. O-O O-O 12. Ne1 Bg4 13. h3 Bh5 14. Ba3 Qa5 15.
Nd3 c4 16. Bxe7 cxd3 17. g4 Nxe7 18. gxh5 Rad8 19. Bxb7 Qb5 20. Bf3 e4 21. Nc3
Qg5+ 22. Bg2 f5 23. e3 Rd6 24. f3 Rh6 25. fxe4 Rxh5 26. Qf3 Nb4 27. exf5 Nxf5
28. e4 Qxd2 29. exf5 Rhxf5 30. Qe4 Rf4 31. Rxf4 Qxc1+ 32. Rf1 d2 33. Qxb4 {
What follows is the game end given by BH Wood (who would have been present at
the venue, if not in the hall):} h6 {"While he was making his 33rd move,
Taimanov's clock flag fell (the time-limit is 34 moves per two hours) so he
forfeited the game. He was, of course, hope­lessly lost. He had run terribly
short of time seven or eight moves before." (Source: BH Wood, Birmingham Daily
Post - Wednesday 04 January 1956; and also Illustrated London News - Saturday
14 January 1956)} (33... Rc8 34. Nd1 {(lost on time) is the end of game given
in the Manchester Guardian, 31 December 1955 and the Sunday Times, 29 January
1956.}) 1-0

